    2. Build a horizontally-symmetric GREY core (8-20 pixels) by placing random pixels and their mirrors; cluster some near the center for blob-like shapes
    3. Sprinkle 5-7 additional GREY noise pixels that do NOT have their mirror also grey (reject or skip if mirror already set)
    4. Verify GREY count is 14-27 and both paired/unpaired subsets are non-empty
    5. Output = copy input, recolor paired grey pixels to BLUE
